Python adaptation and new integration code: grasp-metaskills contributors, 2026.
Modifications include unified Pydantic contracts, immutable graph skill snapshots,
SQLite FTS5 adaptation, injectable execution/providers, concurrency, checked local
repair, version mapping and crash-safe dual-store transactions. Algorithm-specific
ports retain the source revisions identified above. Additional changes include
Python 3.11 module separation, declarative Skills/MCP configuration, an explicit
tool execution bridge, versioned source-resource snapshots, and an independent
provider-injected Meta planning module.

This is an unofficial port of the skill-dag repository's reproduction, not an
official implementation of the GraSP paper and not affiliated with Tencent.
No algorithms from the auxiliary Ericbai06/SkillDAG or wondelai/skills repositories
are incorporated. No model, ONNX asset, UI or host-harness runtime is distributed.
